From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0975 redfin: scanout slots for backboardd's framebuffer surfaces; p mdp ca

Step (d) of docs/redfin/scanout-plan.md. With boot-arg sweetscanout=1|2,
backboardd's 1125x2436 BGRA one-plane surfaces get physically contiguous
memory the display engine reads directly (its apps-SMMU bank has translation
off, r35a): slot 0 in the splash carve-out at 0xa1400000, slots 1-6
contiguous RAM below 4 GB, made on first use and kept. p mdp ca [SLOT [SECS]]
shows the surface in a slot through the scalers (a still frame) and puts the
pipes back after SECS. p mdp test/scale refuse while slot 0 holds a surface.
Inert without the boot-arg.
---
